<title>SRI LANKA: Hayleys up 2.4 pct on growth prospects.</title>
<headline>Hayleys up 2.4 pct on growth prospects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sri Lankan blue chip conglomerate Hayleys Ltd rose 2.4 percent or 5.75 rupees on prospects of improved corporate performance in 1997, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The group is highly diversified with exposure to the hotel and plantation sectors, which are seen doing well in 1997,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>Hotels are seen doing well due to an upturn in tourism, and plantations are expected to see profit growth on continuing demand for Sri Lanka tea.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
